#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The File Templates plug-in allows you to create files based on other files. "
"You can use any file as a template, which will create a copy of the file "
"with an empty &URL;, or use a special template file which may contain macros "
"to fill in information like your name and email address, the current date "
"and so on, and position the cursor at a convenient position in the new file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore, templates located in the template folder will be presented in "
"the menu item <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New from "
"Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plug-in also provides a method to easily create a new template from an "
"open document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The template folder is part of the &kde; file system, and consists of at "
"least KDEDIR/share/applications/kate/plugins/katefiletemplates/templates and "
"KDEHOME/share/applications/kate/plugins/katefiletemplates/templates. If your "
"KDEDIRS environment variable contains additional directories, those are "
"searched for a similar subdirectory as well. If equally named templates are "
"found, the one in the local (KDEHOME) folder is chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu Structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: filetemplates.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenu>New From Template</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Any File...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Presents you with Open File dialog that allows you to use any file as a "
"template. If the chosen file has the extension <filename>katetemplate</"
"filename> it will be parsed for template information and macros."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: filetemplates.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenu>New From Template</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Use Recent</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Presents a list of files recently used as templates, represented by their "
"&URL;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: filetemplates.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New From Template</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The remainder of submenus contains links to templates. Click a menuitem to "
"create a file as described by the menu item text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: filetemplates.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Manage Templates...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will launch a dialog with a list of all templates found within the "
"template directories, along with options to add, edit or remove templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a &kate; Template"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When creating a file from a template that contain template macros, some "
"macros appears as editable variables in the text. Such variables appears as "
"underlined words in the text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first variable will be selected, so you just have to type to edit it.If "
"the document text contains more instances of the same variable, they are "
"changed as you edit. To move to the next editable variable, press the TAB "
"key. When the last variable is edited, the list is dropped, and your TAB key "
"works as normal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating your own templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new template, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Manage Templates</guimenuitem></menuchoice> Item to launch the "
"template management dialog. In that, click <guibutton>New...</guibutton> to "
"launch the File Template Wizard. You will be asked for an optional file to "
"turn into a template and prompted for template information settings, and a "
"template file will be created for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can create a template manually by adding template "
"information to the top of any file, add text and macros, and save it with "
"the <filename>katetemplate</filename> extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The template menu gets automatically updated if you chose to store your "
"template in the template directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit a template, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Manage Templates...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Select the "
"template you want to work on and click <guibutton>Edit...</guibutton>, and "
"the template file will be opened. Close the dialog, edit the template file "
"as desired, save it and close it. Changes to templates takes immediate "
"effect, you can activate the template to test your changes after saving it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kate; Template Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use files with the extension <filename>katetemplate</filename>, they "
"will be parsed for template information, macros and a cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While reading in the file, the parser keeps lines beginning with the phrase "
"<constant>katetemplate:</constant> and searches them for template "
"information in the form VARIABLENAME=VALUE. The first line not starting with "
"<constant>katetemplate:</constant> will be taken as the start of the "
"template contents. VALUE may contain any character but equal sign (=). Legal "
"variable names are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: filetemplates.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template"
msgstr "Modèl"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the template name, displayed in the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: filetemplates.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group"
msgstr "Grop"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The group places the template in a submenu of the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: filetemplates.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Nom"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the name that will be set for the document, and displayed in the "
"file list and title bar. If the name contains <userinput>%N</userinput> that "
"will be replaced with a number, increasing if more documents has the same "
"name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: filetemplates.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plug-in will try to set the Highlight for the new document to the value "
"of this variable. The value should be the name, as found in the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Highlighting</guimenuitem> "
"</menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: filetemplates.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descripcion"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A short informative description of the template. This is currently used to "
"set a Whatsthis string for the menu item, but may be used for more purposes "
"in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "Author"
msgstr "Autor"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A string identifying the author, for example in the form <userinput>Name &lt;"
"email address&gt;</userinput>. This is currently used to set a Whatsthis "
"string for the menu item, but may be used for more purposes in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template Macros"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While parsing the template contents, macros in the form <userinput>%{NAME}</"
"userinput> or <userinput>${NAME}</userinput> are expanded. If you use the "
"<userinput>$</userinput> prefix, the expanded macro will be treated as a "
"editable variable when a document is created from the template, whereas if "
"you use <userinput>%</userinput> it is not, unless expanding failed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following macros are expanded:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "time"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the current time in your locale format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "date"
msgstr "data"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the current date in short format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "datetime"
msgstr "data e ora"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to the current date and time, formatted as a string according to "
"your locale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "year"
msgstr "annada"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current year as a four digit number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "month"
msgstr "mes"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "The full name of the current month, according to your locale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>day</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the current day of the month."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "hostname"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the 'hostname' of your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "index"
msgstr "indèx"

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to 'i'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "fullname"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your full name, as defined by the owner addressee in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "firstname"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your first name, as defined in the owner addressee in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "lastname"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your last name, as defined in the owner addressee in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: filetemplates.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "email"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your email address, as defined by the owner address in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any macro not in the above list is treated as a editable variable no matter "
"the prefix. If the same variable occurs multiple times in the template, they "
"can be edited at once after creating a document from the template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: filetemplates.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting the cursor position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filetemplates.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The special macro <userinput>${cursor}</userinput> will be replaced with a "
"vertical bar and added to the end of the list of editable variables, "
"independent on its location in the text."
msgstr ""

